-<script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ch3\u003eOverview\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbbott Laboratories is a global healthcare and medical device company. This project was an episodic, interactive storytelling experience focused on how to prevent the next pandemic. The site presented a series of documentary-style episodes filmed on the ground across the globe, paired with interactive content that guided users through the narrative.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eRole\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFront End Developer\u003cbr\u003e\nReact, SCSS, GSAP\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eThe Problem\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAbbott needed a platform that could combine cinematic video production with a digital experience that felt both educational and engaging. The challenge was to structure episodic content in a way that was intuitive to explore, while adding interactive elements that kept users actively involved in the story.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eMy Contribution\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI developed the full front end of the site in React, building out the episodic pages, chapter-based navigation, and responsive layouts that supported high-quality video. SCSS was used to create a modular, scalable styling system that kept the design consistent across all episodes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the core episodic content, I built the interactive quiz section that tested users on what they learned from the videos. GSAP was integrated here to power transitions, animations, and feedback effects, making the quiz a dynamic break in the narrative flow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy combining immersive video-driven storytelling with interactive learning moments, the final site delivered a rich, global perspective on pandemic prevention while keeping users engaged from start to finish.\u003c/p\u003e\n"])</script>
